<details class="backup-restore"><summary>Restore this snapshot</summary><p><strong>Content only</strong> restores pages, releases, shows, band/media references, revision history and website text. Media is merged without deleting newer uploads. <strong>Site data</strong> also restores catalog products and categories, but is refused when payment, customer, consent or inventory records have changed since the snapshot.</p><p>Credentials, external transactions, subscriptions and installation secrets are never silently rolled back. Current database schema must match. An automatic pre-restore copy is created before live database changes.</p><form method="post" class="form-stack"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="id" value="<?=e($row['id'])?>"><input type="hidden" name="action" value="restore"><label class="field-stack">Restore scope<select name="scope"><option value="content">Content only — keep current business records</option><option value="site">Site data — requires unchanged operational records</option></select></label><label class="field-stack">Type RESTORE<input name="confirm_restore" required pattern="RESTORE" autocomplete="off"></label><label class="field-stack">Current owner password<input name="owner_password" type="password" required maxlength="72" autocomplete="current-password"></label><button class="button" type="submit">Restore selected site data</button></form></details>
<details class="backup-restore"><summary>Delete this backup copy</summary><form method="post" class="form-stack"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="id" value="<?=e($row['id'])?>"><input type="hidden" name="action" value="delete"><label class="field-stack">Type DELETE<input name="confirm_delete" required pattern="DELETE" autocomplete="off"></label><label class="field-stack">Current owner password<input name="owner_password" type="password" required maxlength="72" autocomplete="current-password"></label><button class="button secondary" type="submit">Permanently delete selected backup</button></form></details></article><?php endforeach;Spirit\Storefront::pager(compact('page','pages'),'admin/backups/');?></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Import a saved snapshot</h2><p>Select the encrypted archive and enter its separate recovery key. Import verifies the archive but does not restore data or execute uploaded PHP/SQL. Only this installation and matching schema are supported.</p><form method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data" class="form-stack"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="import"><label class="field-stack">Encrypted backup archive<input type="file" name="backup" accept=".sgbackup" required></label><label class="field-stack">64-character recovery key<input name="recovery_key" type="password" minlength="64" maxlength="64" required autocomplete="off"></label><label class="field-stack">Current owner password<input name="owner_password" type="password" required maxlength="72" autocomplete="current-password"></label><button class="button" type="submit">Import and verify backup</button></form></section>
